# Kubetools

Sublime Text 4 plugin: **inline compare** of open Kubernetes YAML to live cluster
state, **seal / unseal** (kubeseal), plus apply / dry-run.

Requires plugin host **Python 3.14** (see `.python-version`; Sublime Text build
with the 3.14 plugin host, typically **≥4169**).

Package folder / Package Control name: **`kubetools`** (must match for Settings menus).

## Commands (Cmd+Shift+P — type `.kube`)

| Command | What it does |
|---------|----------------|
| **.kubetools - Compare State** | Pick context → underline differing values **inline** on the manifest |
| **.kubetools - Clear Compare Overlays** | Remove inline annotations / banner |
| **.kubetools - Apply Open File** | Context → namespace if needed → dry-run + diff + confirm → `kubectl apply` |
| **.kubetools - Dry-Run Open File** | Read-only server-side dry-run |
| **.kubetools - Seal** | Selection → `--raw` encrypt in SealedSecret; no selection → seal Secret → `*-sealedsecret.yaml` |
| **.kubetools - Unseal** | Offline decrypt selection with stage private key → scratch tab (`DO-NOT-COMMIT`, read-only) |

## Seal stages

Configure **`stages` only in Packages/User/Kubetools.sublime-settings** (cert +
optional private key per cluster). Keep **User/Kubeseal.sublime-settings**
`stages` empty so you do not maintain two lists.

If Kubetools `stages` is empty, legacy User `Kubeseal.sublime-settings` is used
as a fallback.

**When GitOps adds** `environments/<env>/<cluster>/sealed-secrets/pub.pem`, add a
stage whose `name` matches `<cluster>`. Run **Validate Seal Config** after edits.
If a cluster uses a **dedicated** Sealed Secrets key, read that cluster’s
`sealed-secrets` docs before reusing sealed YAML from another cluster.

See **[docs/USER-MANUAL.md](../docs/USER-MANUAL.md)** for onboarding and
`context_path_aliases`.

After a full-file seal, you are offered **Compare State** on the sealed file.
Overwriting an existing `*-sealedsecret.yaml` requires confirmation (previous → `.bckp-*`).

### Compare labels

Live values appear on the line **below** each diff (smaller font), not as a
jagged right-hand column (Sublime cannot do that reliably).

- `live | *** | copy` — cluster has a value (Secret fields redacted); template differs
- `live | absent` — key is not on the live object
- Secrets: `stringData.*` is matched to live `data.*`

## Read-only guarantee (Compare / Diff / Dry-Run)

These modes **cannot** mutate the open file, buffer text (only overlays), or the
cluster without `--dry-run`. Temp files stay under the system temp dir.

**Apply** and **Seal** are the only modes that write (cluster / sealed sibling).

## Apply safety locks (cannot be disabled)

- Always pass explicit `--context`
- Always `kubectl apply --dry-run=server` before real apply
- Always require quick-panel confirmation
- Never `--force` / `--force-conflicts`
- Frozen buffer snapshot via temp file (`0600`)
- One interactive flow at a time

## Keyboard (default chords)

Press **ctrl+k**, then (only in **YAML / JSON** buffers — avoids stealing ST’s
global `ctrl+k` chords):

| Chord | Action |
|-------|--------|
| **h** | Hub (all actions) |
| **c** | Compare State |
| **d** | Dry-Run |
| **a** | Apply (still full confirms) |
| **s** / **u** | Seal / Unseal |
| **n** / **p** | Next / Prev diff |
| **y** | Copy live under caret |
| **x** | Clear overlays |
| **,** | Settings |

Remap: Preferences → Package Settings → Kubetools → Key Bindings.

Panels: **Enter** confirms highlighted item, **Esc** cancels. On dangerous apply,
**Cancel is listed first** so accidental Enter aborts.

## Context preselect (safe)

When the open file path contains a cluster folder (e.g.
`environments/dev/my-cluster/...`), that kubectl context is **highlighted** in the
context quick panel. The panel is **always** shown — never skipped.

- Apply still requires dry-run + confirm (+ type-to-confirm on prod-like names)
- Compare / Dry-Run never mutate the cluster or the open file
- Settings: `guess_context_from_path`, `context_path_aliases`

**Preferences → Package Settings → Kubetools → Settings** (Default | User), or
Command Palette → `.kubetools - Settings`.

Put your seal `stages` (cert / private key paths) in **Settings – User** only.
Opening Kubetools Settings can one-time migrate from old User Kubeseal settings;
then clear Kubeseal `stages` to avoid duplication.

## Requirements

- Sublime Text 4 (Build 4205+)
- `kubectl` on PATH (or set `kubectl_path`)
- `kubeseal` on PATH for Seal/Unseal (or set `kubeseal_path`)
